this lesson we're going to talk about  unit conversions so understanding how to  convert from one unit to another unit  using unit conversions is an important  concept to understand for the act and  what we're doing is we're going to go  through an example see if you can do  this one on your own we'll go through it  together  it says if a 20 inch diameter wheel okay  rotates at 50 revolutions per minute how  many feet does a point on the outer edge  of the wheel travel in one hour so let's  just draw a diagram here so here's the  wheel it's a 20 inch diameter wheel and  we're looking at a point on the outer  edge you know how far does it travel  okay um you know if it's rotating at 50  revolutions per minute  how far would it travel in one hour so  let's start with it with what they give  us which is the 50 revolutions  per one minute right  so every time this wheel goes once  around okay that's one revolution it  travels the circumference of the circle  and remember circumference is 2 pi r  or pi times diameter so in this case it  would be 20 pi inches so 20 pi inches  now you know you're on the right track  because the units that you don't want  are going to cancel out numerator and  denominator so now we're into inches but  we want to figure out how far is it  going to travel in one hour well  okay let's see we're trying to figure  out how many uh  feet does it travel so first thing let's  travel let's translate from inches to  feet so we know that there's 12 inches  in every one foot and i set it up this  way so that the inches will cancel with  the inches and we have feet okay and  we've got minutes so feet per minute but  we're trying to figure out how many feet  does it travel in one hour so we have to  convert the minutes now to hours so  there's for every 60 minutes there's one  hour oops one hr one hour so you can see  the minutes are cancelling numerator and  denominator and we're left with feet  per hour per means like divided by right  so number of feet divided by the number  of hours so now all we have to do is  multiply all the numerators together all  the denominators together and then  divide and that's going to be our end  result so i'm going to go ahead and do  that on the calculator just so we know  what the answer is it's 50  times 20 times pi which is 3.14 you can  use your pi key times 60 okay all  divided by 1 times 1 times 12 times 1  which is 12 so divided by 12 and that  comes out to  15 000 okay 15  707  well we'll round it to 708 so it's about  15 708 feet and you've got it so  basically unit conversions are all about  you know recognizing that you know  working with fractions the numerator and  denominator those units are going to  cancel and you're going to switch from  one unit to the next unit to the next  unit until you get the units that you  want so definitely an important concept  to understand i'll see you in the next  lesson
 

